+#
+# spec_variant:
+#   preserved_structure:
+#     grid: square 20-30
+#     palette: black background + exactly 2 large non-black/non-teal regions
+#     cleanup: unchanged 2-pass local cleanup removes isolated fg specks and
+#       one-cell boundary protrusions before any dent reasoning
+#   changed_core:
+#     dent_detection_unit: black dent connected components in the candidate-dent
+#       mask, not independent black pixels
+#     legal_dent_shapes:
+#       - 1 cell
+#       - 2 horizontally adjacent cells
+#       - 2 vertically adjacent cells
+#     output_mapping:
+#       - 1-cell dent -> standard opposite-color 3x3 patch, center teal
+#       - horizontal 2-cell dent -> opposite-color horizontal bar of length 3;
+#         the bar contains the two teal cells and extends one extra cell toward
+#         the side with stronger host support in the cleaned grid
+#       - vertical 2-cell dent -> analogous vertical length-3 bar
+#   behavior_trace:
+#     original_local_case: |
+#       If two adjacent black dent cells appear inside one region, the original
+#       solver treats them as two separate centers and stamps two overlapping
+#       3x3 patches, producing a 3x4 or 4x3 blob.
+#     new_local_case: |
+#       The same adjacent pair is first grouped as one dent component. Its shape
+#       is classified by the component bbox: 1x2 means horizontal, 2x1 means
+#       vertical. The solver then stamps one thin opposite-color stripe aligned
+#       with that axis, and all original dent cells become teal.
+#     visible_difference: |
+#       The output is no longer only "3x3 around each teal cell". Some teal
+#       pairs now sit inside thin 3-long bars, so shape-to-shape mapping is
+#       visible directly in the output.
+#   implicit_assumption_audit:
+#     - _clean_foreground still assumes noise is one-cell corruption only; this
+#       remains valid because the variant changes only dent geometry.
+#     - old _dent_centers assumed every black candidate cell should be processed
+#       independently. This is invalid once 2-cell dents are meaningful units.
+#     - old main overwrote a 3x3 patch for every detected cell. In the variant,
+#       unconditional per-cell 3x3 stamping would destroy the required thin-bar
+#       outputs for 2-cell dents.
+#     - the new bar-placement rule assumes a 2-cell dent has a meaningful
+#       stronger-support side. The generator therefore prefers pair dents whose
+#       left/right or up/down bar candidates receive different support scores.
+#   placement_legality:
+#     - dent groups are selected with Chebyshev distance >= 3 between every pair
+#       of black dent cells across groups, so local neighborhoods do not
+#       interfere and 3x3 patches stay visually separable.
+#     - pair dents are generated only when both cells remain candidate dents
+#       after blackening the whole pair, and when the induced bar is supported
+#       by the host region.
+#   observability:
+#     - each generated puzzle targets at least one horizontal pair and one
+#       vertical pair when candidate supply permits, so the D12 branch is
+#       represented in the training distribution instead of degenerating to the
+#       original all-3x3 behavior.
+#     - only geometric cues drive the branch choice; color ids are never used.
+#   cleanliness:
+#     - output marks remain limited to opposite-color patches plus teal dent
